  "notes": "FORMS:\n{融|ゆう} (dissolve, melt) + {解|かい} (dissolve, undo) → melting/dissolving\n{融解|ゆうかい}する (to melt, to fuse)\n\nSCIENTIFIC TERMS:\n- {融解|ゆうかい}{点|てん} (melting point)\n- {融解|ゆうかい}{熱|ねつ} (heat of fusion)\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {溶解|ようかい} (dissolution - dissolving in a liquid)\n- {凝固|ぎょうこ} (solidification - antonym)\n- {蒸発|じょうはつ} (evaporation)\n- {凝縮|ぎょうしゅく} (condensation)\n\nUSAGE:\n{融解|ゆうかい} refers specifically to the phase change from solid to liquid, while {溶解|ようかい} refers to dissolving a substance in a solvent.",
